    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Yeah, documentation should be the main thing. But look, I've been looking at the progress on the refactoring. The current modularization is getting pretty deep, and I'm worried that if we just \"document\" it and then switch to a totally different architecture, the new model won't actually be able to maintain the performance levels we've hit. \n\nThere are a lot of highly optimized, non-standard logic flows in the Polaris core that are really dependent on how you've been structuring the code. Do you think a generic AI-native model can actually handle the nuances of this codebase, or is there a risk that the migration will basically break everything?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
